			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-962428">
									

<p>To me, this screamed "SCP-version of Phillip Pullman's daemons<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-521998-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-521998-1')">1</a></sup> with the Specters thrown in for a measure of creepy". Everything matches up: pre-pubescent children only, can change shape, the Rabbit-Specters devour the other daemons, leaving their owners in a coma.</p>
<p>But it works! The images are good (are they done via light painting? Some of them look like it), and though the tone <em>is</em> off at times, the writeup is rather good. I also like the notion that it's not only the kids controlling the 'sketches', but sometimes vice-versa.</p>
