<p>I'm going to try to get around to editing this extensively over the next few days for the major points brought up; tone, clarity, redaction, and overall readability structure if I can figure out what needs to be done about that.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>In my opinion, if Area I-4 = SCP-277 then you don't really need to specify Area I-4.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I had some problems deciding what to designate what, as it's ambiguous whether the physical land itself is the source of the sketches. Personally, I liked referring to it as Area I-4 for some reason. You think it would work if I shifted the designation of the sketches themselves to SCP-277?<br />
By the way, the kid wasn't supposed to come off as possessed. There ought to have been some uncertainty around whether it really was a psychopathic kid, or whether something was persuading him to lie as part of some kind of game or whatnot. So that goes on the 'needs editing' list as well.<br />
His Dark Materials is an awesome trilogy. Weird how I didn't catch the correlation, actually, but the edit'll make the difference it bit more clear.<br />
…Dexanote, dammit, now I can't get that idea out of my head. &gt;&lt;</p>

